-- W9 port of test/llvm_fixtures_modules/record_xmod_field_type_swap/entry.mdk
-- (#1418) — the `ws:soundness` half of #1382 (fixed): same mechanism as
-- `record_xmod_field_order/`, but the two colliding fields have DIFFERENT TYPES at
-- the swapped positions, so the wrong slot is not just the wrong number: it reads
-- an `Int` out of a cell holding a `String` pointer. On the LLVM backend, pre-fix
-- this shape was a native segfault rather than a wrong-value print (recorded in
-- the LLVM original's own comment) — the class of bug a backend can get wrong in
-- a way an interpreter structurally cannot, which is exactly why it belongs in
-- every backend's corpus, wasm included.
--
-- Expected output, derived BY HAND from the sources before this fixture was ever
-- run, identically to the already-hand-derived LLVM original:
--   zrmod: mkZ = Cfg { s = "zed", a = 44 }  =>  zrOut = "44" ++ "zed" = 44zed
--   armod: mkA = Cfg { a = 11, s = "arm" }  =>  arOut = "11" ++ "arm" = 11arm
-- so `44zed|11arm`.
--
-- Live differential (native oracle) gate — no golden to enshrine. Checked against
-- the hand-derived value above, not just against each other.
import armod.{arOut}
import zrmod.{zrOut}

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (zrOut ++ "|" ++ arOut)
